 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nTeradata dialect broken after recent changes\n\nDescription\n\nThe Teradata dialect is throwing UnboundLocalError and other errors when parsing certain SQL expressions. This affects date/time operations and TRANSLATE statements.\n\nSteps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\n\n# This should work but throws UnboundLocalError\nsqlglot.transpile(\"SELECT '2023-01-01' + INTERVAL '5' YEAR\", read=\"teradata\", write=\"snowflake\")\n\n# This should also work but throws parsing errors  \nsqlglot.transpile(\"TRANSLATE(x USING LATIN_TO_UNICODE)\", read=\"teradata\", write=\"teradata\")\n\n# Extract quarter functionality is also broken\nsqlglot.transpile(\"EXTRACT(QUARTER FROM x)\", read=\"teradata\", write=\"bigquery\")\n```\n\nThe errors seem to be related to variable references before assignment in the Teradata dialect implementation. Date arithmetic and character set translation operations are particularly affected.\n</issue>\n",
